<title>USA: Stiglitz to resign as CEA chief to join World Bank.</title>
<headline>Stiglitz to resign as CEA chief to join World Bank.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Joseph Stiglitz plans to resign as chairman of the White House Council of Economic Advisers to become chief economist of the World Bank, the White House said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Stiglitz, 53, a former Stanford faculty member, has served as CEA chairman for the past 18 months.  The timing of his departure remains to be determined, officials said.</p>
<p>Stiglitz's exit creates a seventh vacancy in President Clinton's economic policy cluster. Possible replacements include CEA member Alicia Munnell and Princeton economist Alan Blinder, officials said.</p>
</text>
